C. Imitation learning-based Explanations
Similar to RL-based explanations, IL-based explanations also provide insights from an algorithmic perspective regarding how an IL agent makes decisions. Cultrera et al. ’s work [95] is one of the preliminary studies in this context. The study uses a conditional IL agent along with the attention model in the CARLA simulator [96] to produce an explanation describing the influence of distinctive parts of the driving images on the predictions of the model. Further works include NEAT [97], model-based IL (MILE) [98], Hierarchical Interpretable Imitation Learning (HIIL) [99], PlanT [100], and generative adversarial network (GAN)-based IL approach combined with signal temporal logic (STL) [101].

