Shahin Atakishiyev is from the Mirzabayli village of Gabala, Azerbaijan. He received a PhD in Computing Science in September 2024 and an MSc in Software Engineering and Intelligent Systems in January 2018 from the University of Alberta, Canada. He obtained a BSc in Computer Engineering from Qafqaz University, Azerbaijan, in June 2015. During his doctoral study, Shahin built explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) approaches for autonomous vehicles under the supervision of Prof. Randy Goebel. His research interests include safe, ethical, humancentered, and explainable artificial intelligence applied to real-world problems.

